      "writtenOn": "2020-05-28T11:46:27Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This is done because if there is a downstream, Tethering would not stop and you would keep getting notifications about upstreams right ?\nThis is building logic of this class based on implementation details of Tethering, which should not be done (because someone changing Tethering won\u0027t know that it breaks the logic here).\n\nCould you instead just call this method from Tethering when it knows that it is starting with no downstream ? Or alternatively always do the cleanup.",
